OCR and Types of OCR
Optical Character Recognition (OCR)

OCR (Optical Character Recognition) is a technology that converts text present in images,
scanned documents, and PDF files into machine-readable text. In UiPath, OCR enables robots to read and process documents automatically without manual data entry.

Example:
 A scanned invoice can be converted into text containing Invoice Number, Supplier Name, Invoice Date, and Total Amount.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Types of OCR
1. Tesseract OCR

Tesseract OCR is an open-source OCR engine used to recognize text from scanned images and documents.

Features:

Open-source and free to use.
Developed by HP and later maintained by Google.
Supports multiple languages.
Can run locally without cloud connectivity.
Suitable for clear and high-quality printed text.

Example:
 Reading invoice numbers, supplier names, and amounts from scanned invoices.

2. Microsoft OCR

Microsoft OCR is a cloud-based OCR service provided through Microsoft 
Azure that extracts text using Artificial Intelligence.

Features:

Cloud-based OCR service.
Uses AI-based image recognition.
Supports multiple languages.
Can process printed and handwritten text.
Suitable for complex documents and images.
Requires Azure credentials and internet access.

Example:
 Extracting text from scanned application forms and business documents.

3. Google Cloud OCR

Google Cloud OCR is a cloud-based OCR service provided by Google
Cloud that uses Machine Learning and Computer Vision technologies.

Features:

Cloud-based OCR service.
Uses Machine Learning and Computer Vision.
Supports printed and handwritten text recognition.
Detects text from images and scanned documents.
Provides advanced document text recognition.
Requires Google Cloud API access and credentials.

Example:
 Extracting text from scanned receipts, invoices, and forms.

